      "link": "https://english.pravda.ru/news/world/170790-uganda-ebola-quarantine/",
      "title": "Uganda imposes 21-day quarantine on arrivals from Congo to block Ebola spread",
      "description": "Uganda has mandated a 21-day quarantine for its citizens returning from the Democratic Republic of Congo, a measure announced by Health Minister Chris Baryomunsi to tighten Ebola precautions. The decision comes despite Uganda officially declaring its latest Ebola outbreak over in July, and follows recent positive tests among travelers who passed through the country. The quarantine requirement applies specifically to Ugandan nationals who have recently traveled to the DRC, the region where the current outbreak is active. Health officials state that all travelers entering Uganda by air, land, or water must now complete a passenger locator form, while screening at Entebbe International Airport and land border crossings has been intensified. This escalation is driven by two recent cases that raised concerns about transmission routes. In Kenya, a patient who traveled from the Congo through Uganda to Nairobi died two days after arrival. In Nigeria, a 42-year-old woman, identified as the wife of a Swiss diplomat, tested positive after returning from Uganda via Addis Ababa to Abuja on October 3. Nigeria's Centre for Disease Control reported that she is in isolation and has improved remarkably, with 53 contacts traced.",
